{Spin2_v50}
'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_bench_char.spin2
''   Purpose.... Early motor characterisation binary -- quarter/half-speed, constant-rate,
''               forward and reverse, hold-and-announce on a live PLOT panel
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 11 Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 11 Sep 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHY THIS RUN, AND WHY NOW

  This runs BEFORE the current-scaling and hall-counting fixes land. Almost nothing it
  measures is invalidated by those pending fixes -- the S-3 restore divides sense_i_mV by a
  constant, the board-detection fix touches getCurrent() but not raw sense_i_mV, the hall
  counters are purely additive, tickInMM_x10 changes distance conversion but not raw ticks --
  and a constant scale error hides neither a ratio, an asymmetry, nor a shape. Quarter speed
  (~100 ticks/s against a 43.9kHz control loop) makes pos as trustworthy as it will ever be.

  WHAT THIS BUYS, most valuable first:
   (1) turns the S-3 adc_fram=6136 prediction into a measurement, before anything is built on
       it -- log raw sense_i_mV, Stephen reads meter amps, the ratio should land near 6136;
   (2) forward-vs-reverse asymmetry (the reverse offset is derived, 360-43, never measured);
   (3) a go/no-go on the current channel itself -- is it alive and load-responsive at all;
   (4) left/right hardware equivalence at matched commanded rate.

  THE CONDITION THIS RUN IS ACCEPTED UNDER: record raw values AS RAW. Ratios, asymmetries and
  liveness are fair game; absolute magnitudes are logged with the scale factor UNRESOLVED and
  converted afterward, never asserted during the session. sense_i_mV on the panel is
  deliberately demoted -- labelled "P2 SENSE mV", never "amps", never converted -- so it
  answers "is this hold real" without anchoring Stephen's meter transcription.

  DELIBERATELY NOT ATTEMPTED: the fault boundary, anything depending on stop distance, rpm or
  cntsInSec (broken, finding W), getCurrent() absolute, high speed.

  THE IDLE WHEEL FLOATS BY CONSTRUCTION. The wheel not under test is never start()ed at all --
  no driver cog, pins left as inputs, bridges off -- rather than started and told to hold.
  holdAtStop() appears nowhere in this file; init()'s own default (SM_FLOAT) already gives a
  floating stop, so there is nothing to call.

  NO STOP TIMER. util_char_motor.spin2:379,392 call stopAfterTime(DRIVE_AT_SPEED_SECS=5, ...)
  before every drive -- an operator hold is indefinite, and that timer would stop the motor
  five seconds in while the panel kept looking correct. This file commands motion with
  testDriveAtMotorIncrement() alone and never calls stopAfterTime() from a hold.

  PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY. emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in
  about 250 ms (finding S-4) and is NOT a panic button; this file does not call it.

  HOW IT IS RUN

      cd src
      pnut-ts -l -d -D BENCH_CFG test_bench_char.spin2      ' the bench PLOT panel
      pnut-ts -l -d -D BENCH_NO_PANEL test_bench_char.spin2 ' plain debug-line fallback

  -D BENCH_CFG selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2 for the banner's cfg_id only --
  the pin bases, voltage and detection mode this file actually drives are hardcoded (see CON
  { bench target } below) so this file compiles and drives the same fixed hardware regardless
  of which block happens to be active in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2, exactly the reasoning
  test_bench_t0.spin2 documents at its own T0_MOTOR_BASE.

  -D BENCH_NO_PANEL opens a bare PLOT window (needed only so pc_key has a window to read from)
  with no drawing at all, and prints the prompt and counter as plain debug lines instead.
  Nothing that matters may exist only on the panel -- every BC- log record is identical
  between the two builds.

  RECORD DISCIPLINE

  Tag-first, comma-separated name,value pairs, all tags prefixed BC-. Fixed-field: every
  record type always emits every field in the same order; absence is a TOKEN (NOMEAS / NA /
  NEVER), never a missing field and never a 0. Records are assembled into a byte buffer and
  emitted with one debug(zstr_()) each, because a single DEBUG statement carries at most 255
  bytes and several of these records would overrun that. The line-assembly idiom
  (lineReset/lineAddText/lineAddNum/lineField/lineTextField/lineEmit) is transcribed from
  test_bench_detect.spin2, which cannot be OBJ-included because it is itself a top-level file.

  THE STRUCTURAL GUARANTEE

  Exactly one statement in this file assigns the dwell-gate flag -- comparing elapsed
  milliseconds since steady state against the dwell floor -- inside the poll loop of
  runDwellLoop() below. No input path (mouse, keyboard, or the BENCH_NO_PANEL keyboard path)
  may set that flag -- all three write only bAdvanceRequested, and a hold advances only when
  the gate flag AND bAdvanceRequested are both true.
}

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV     = 1                                         ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes
    FMT_VERSION = 1                                          ' BC-BANNER record-format version

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' every top in this tree runs at 270 MHz
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    MS_PER_SEC = 1000

CON { bench target -- the fixed dual 6.5in Rev B 18.5V rig }

' Hardcoded rather than read from `user`, for the same reason test_bench_t0.spin2 hardcodes
' T0_MOTOR_BASE: a dual-motor active config block defines LEFT_MOTOR_BASE/RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE
' and no ONLY_MOTOR_BASE, and vice versa for a single-motor block, so reading either through
' `user` would fail to compile under whichever block happens to be active. This file needs
' BOTH a left and a right base, so it names the library's own PINS_*/PWR_*/BRD_* constants
' directly -- legal under every config block, because they belong to the isp_bldc_motor
' object, not to the user config.
    LEFT_TEST_BASE  = wheelL.PINS_P32_P47                    ' the LEFT board is at P32, measured 2026-09-11
    RIGHT_TEST_BASE = wheelL.PINS_P16_P31
    TEST_VOLTAGE    = wheelL.PWR_18p5V
    TEST_DET_MODE   = wheelL.BRD_AUTO_DET
    PACK_NOMINAL_MV = 18_500                                ' 5S pack, nominal -- Stephen states the true value at the meter

CON { drive speed }

' isp_bldc_motor.spin2:1202 -- ~147_000_000 is the motor-increment ceiling at 18.5V.
    DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE = 147_000_000
    QTR_SPEED_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 4           ' ~36_750_000, quarter speed
    HALF_SPEED_INCRE    = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 2           ' ~73_500_000, optional second rung

CON { dwell / steady-state timing }

    DWELL_FLOOR_SECS       = 25                             ' 5 meter screens x ~4s + margin
    STEADY_SAMPLE_MS        = 250
    STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES  = 4
    STEADY_TOL_PCT          = 5
    STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS       = 6_000
    EARLY_FLASH_MS          = 300
    BTN_ACK_HOLD_MS         = 250
    DWELL_POLL_MS           = 50                             ' input + panel poll cadence
    PANEL_REDRAW_MS         = 200                            ' throttled panel redraw cadence
    SENSE_MEAN_UPDATE_MS    = 1_000                          ' on-screen sense mV update cadence
    IDLE_SHOW_MS            = 4_000                          ' completion screen dwell before the session ends
    PREFLIGHT_MS            = 700                            ' nudge duration per wheel in the pre-flight check
    PREFLIGHT_INCRE         = 18_375_000                     ' half of quarter speed -- enough to turn, gentle
    MAX_CLICK_LOG           = 5                              ' BC-CLICK is "first clicks", not every click

CON ' ---- Hold Sequence ----
  ' The nine-hold run: quiescent zero, then left/right x fwd/rev at quarter speed, then
  ' left/right x fwd/rev again at half speed. HOLD_LAST selects how far the run actually
  ' goes; default is the whole sequence.
    #0, HOLD_ZERO, HOLD_L_FWD_QTR, HOLD_L_REV_QTR, HOLD_R_FWD_QTR, HOLD_R_REV_QTR, ...
        HOLD_L_FWD_HALF, HOLD_L_REV_HALF, HOLD_R_FWD_HALF, HOLD_R_REV_HALF
    HOLD_COUNT = HOLD_R_REV_HALF + 1
    HOLD_LAST  = HOLD_R_REV_HALF                            ' edit to stop the run earlier

CON ' ---- Motor-Side / Button / Result Enums ----
  ' Which wheel (if any) is under test:
  '  SIDE_NONE  - neither wheel started (the quiescent-zero hold)
  '  SIDE_LEFT  - wheelL started, wheelR never started (floating)
  '  SIDE_RIGHT - wheelR started, wheelL never started (floating)
    #0, SIDE_NONE, SIDE_LEFT, SIDE_RIGHT

  ' Panel button visual states:
  '  PNL_BTN_INERT - dwell floor not yet reached, click/keypress ignored
  '  PNL_BTN_LIVE  - floor reached, waiting for the operator's acknowledgement
  '  PNL_BTN_ACK   - acknowledgement just accepted, brief visible feedback
    #0, PNL_BTN_INERT, PNL_BTN_LIVE, PNL_BTN_ACK

  ' Steady-state source, hold outcome, and advance-source tokens are carried as string
  ' pointers (see DAT token strings below) rather than numeric enums, since they go straight
  ' into BC- log fields.

CON { panel geometry -- see file header table; sizes chosen for arm's-length legibility }

    HDR_X = 0,   HDR_Y = 0,   HDR_W = 640, HDR_H = 44
    CAP_X = 16,  CAP_Y = 52,  CAP_W = 608, CAP_H = 48
    MODE_X = 16, MODE_Y = 110, MODE_W = 268, MODE_H = 44
    CNT_X = 16,  CNT_Y = 164, CNT_W = 236, CNT_H = 104
    BAR_X = 16,  BAR_Y = 272, BAR_W = 236, BAR_H = 14
    BTN_X = 300, BTN_Y = 150, BTN_W = 316, BTN_H = 120
    CHIP_X = 16, CHIP_Y = 286, CHIP_W = 268, CHIP_H = 44
    SNS_X = 300, SNS_Y = 286, SNS_W = 316, SNS_H = 44
    FOOT_X = 0,  FOOT_Y = 340, FOOT_W = 640, FOOT_H = 60

    PANEL_W = 640
    PANEL_H = 400
    PANEL_POS_X = 60
    PANEL_POS_Y = 80

    ' Layer/cell geometry -- GENERATED by tools/gen_bench_char_assets.py. That script draws the
    ' BMPs from these same numbers and prints this block, so artwork and code cannot drift.
    LYR_BG           = 1
    LYR_CAP          = 2
    LYR_DGT          = 3
    LYR_LBL          = 4
    LYR_BTN          = 5

    DGT_X            = 16
    DGT_Y            = 164
    DGT_W            = 72
    DGT_H            = 104
    DGT_PITCH        = 82
    DGT_COUNT        = 3
    DGT_BLANK        = 10
    DGT_ROW_NORM     = 0
    DGT_ROW_FLASH    = 104

    LBL_W            = 268
    LBL_H            = 44
    LBL_MODE_DWELL   = 0
    LBL_MODE_HELD    = 1
    LBL_STAT_ZERO    = 2
    LBL_STAT_RUN     = 3
    LBL_STAT_FAULT   = 4

    TXTSTYLE_CENTER    = 0                                  ' halign/valign both center (default)
    TXTSTYLE_LEFT_MID  = $30                                ' halign left (%11<<4), valign center

CON { panel feature flags }

    PNL_SHOW_SENSE = 1                                      ' one-constant removal per spec

CON { record assembly buffer }

    LINE_BUF_SIZE    = 640
    MAX_DEC_DIGITS   = 11
    DEC_RADIX        = 10
    DIGITS_PER_GROUP = 3

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user   : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"              ' banner cfg_id only -- see CON { bench target }
#else
    user   : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"
#endif
    wheelL : "isp_bldc_motor"                                ' left wheel instance
    wheelR : "isp_bldc_motor"                                ' right wheel instance

DAT { record assembly state }

lineBuf         BYTE    0[LINE_BUF_SIZE]
lineLen         LONG    0

DAT { token strings }

sMotNone        BYTE    "NONE", 0
sMotLeft        BYTE    "LEFT", 0
sMotRight       BYTE    "RIGHT", 0

sDirZero        BYTE    "ZERO", 0
sDirFwd         BYTE    "FWD", 0
sDirRev         BYTE    "REV", 0

sRungZero       BYTE    "ZERO", 0
sRungQtr        BYTE    "QTR", 0
sRungHalf       BYTE    "HALF", 0

sSteadyRamped   BYTE    "RAMPED", 0
sSteadyTimeout  BYTE    "TIMEOUT", 0
sSteadyZerocmd  BYTE    "ZEROCMD", 0

sAdvMouse       BYTE    "MOUSE", 0
sAdvKey         BYTE    "KEY", 0
sAdvKeynp       BYTE    "KEYNP", 0

sResultOk       BYTE    "OK", 0
sResultFault    BYTE    "FAULT", 0

sInZoneYes      BYTE    "1", 0
sInZoneNo       BYTE    "0", 0

sPanelYes       BYTE    "YES", 0
sPanelNo        BYTE    "NO", 0

sCfgBench       BYTE    "BENCH", 0
sCfgUser        BYTE    "USER", 0

sStatZero       BYTE    "ZERO COMMAND", 0
sStatRunning    BYTE    "MOTOR RUNNING", 0
sStatFault      BYTE    "DRIVER FAULT", 0

sModeDwell      BYTE    "DWELL REMAINING", 0
sModeHeld       BYTE    "HELD - SEC", 0

DAT { hold caption strings }

sHold0Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 1 of 9 - QUIESCENT ZERO", 0
sHold1Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 2 of 9 - LEFT WHEEL FORWARD - 1/4 SPEED", 0
sHold2Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 3 of 9 - LEFT WHEEL REVERSE - 1/4 SPEED", 0
sHold3Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 4 of 9 - RIGHT WHEEL FORWARD - 1/4 SPEED", 0
sHold4Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 5 of 9 - RIGHT WHEEL REVERSE - 1/4 SPEED", 0
sHold5Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 6 of 9 - LEFT WHEEL FORWARD - 1/2 SPEED", 0
sHold6Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 7 of 9 - LEFT WHEEL REVERSE - 1/2 SPEED", 0
sHold7Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 8 of 9 - RIGHT WHEEL FORWARD - 1/2 SPEED", 0
sHold8Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 9 of 9 - RIGHT WHEEL REVERSE - 1/2 SPEED", 0

VAR { mouse read -- pc_mouse fills these 7 adjacent longs in this exact order }

    LONG    mouseXpos
    LONG    mouseYpos
    LONG    mouseWheelDelta
    LONG    mouseLtButton
    LONG    mouseMidButton
    LONG    mouseRtButton
    LONG    mousePixel

VAR { keyboard read }

    LONG    keyCode

VAR { run-wide state }

    LONG    currentSide                                     ' SIDE_* -- which wheel (if any) has a running cog
    LONG    prevMouseLt                                      ' previous poll's left-button reading, for edge detect
    LONG    bKeyArmed                                         ' TRUE once keyCode has read 0 since the last accepted press
    LONG    clickLogCount                                     ' BC-CLICK emitted so far, this whole run

PUB main()
'' Run the whole bench characterisation sequence: quiescent zero, then each wheel forward and
'' reverse at quarter and (optionally) half speed, hold-and-announce on every step.
''

    currentSide := SIDE_NONE
    prevMouseLt := 0
    bKeyArmed := TRUE
    clickLogCount := 0

    setupWindow()
    emitBanner()
    if not preflightWheels()
        debug("! ABORTING -- see BC-PREFLIGHT above. Fix the wiring or the declared pin group,")
        debug("!   then re-run. Running nine holds against a wheel that cannot turn wastes the session.")
        shutdownMotors()
        debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
        return
    runAllHolds()
    shutdownMotors()

    ' Draw the completion screen once, leave it up long enough to read, then emit the marker
    ' and stop. The previous shape looped forever redrawing it, so --exit-on-end-session never
    ' fired: the terminal had to be killed by hand and the log never closed cleanly.
    ' QUOTED, not backticked -- a backtick makes it a display command and the marker is missed.
    drawIdlePanel()
    waitms(IDLE_SHOW_MS)
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")

PRI setupWindow()
' Open the PLOT window once. Screen-native Y-down (CARTESIAN 1, per ruling R2) so the zone
' table in the file header is valid as written, and so pc_mouse's cursor_coordinate reports
' in the same basis this file draws in -- no inversion needed for the button hit test.
' hidexy suppresses the measurement-cursor readout; it does not disable pc_mouse.
' Opened identically in both builds -- BENCH_NO_PANEL just never draws into it afterward.

    ' LITERALS, not `(PANEL_W, PANEL_H) -- see the note above this method. These four numbers
    ' MUST equal PANEL_W / PANEL_H / PANEL_POS_X / PANEL_POS_Y. A mismatch is detectable rather
    ' than silent: BC-BANNER emits the CON values and pnut-term-ts logs its own WINDOW_PLACED
    ' line with the size it actually opened, so the two can be compared in any log.
    debug(`PLOT bench TITLE 'P2-BLDC bench characterisation' SIZE 640 400 POS 60 80 HIDEXY UPDATE)

    ' Bitmap layers, loaded once. This is the crop-and-overlay technique from
    ' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/, as demonstrated by test_dog_panel.spin2:486-492 --
    ' a panel known to work on this bench. No CARTESIAN: that reference does not use it, crop
    ' coordinates are image coordinates already, and pc_mouse then reports in the same basis the
    ' reference hit-tests in. Filenames are bare, so the terminal's cwd must be src/ -- which is
    ' what tools/bench-run.sh does.
    debug(`bench LAYER 1 'bc_bg.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 2 'bc_caption.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 3 'bc_digits.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 4 'bc_labels.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 5 'bc_button.bmp')
    debug(`bench CROP 1)
    debug(`bench UPDATE)

PRI emitBanner()
' Emit BC-BANNER once. cfg_id and panel are each sourced from their own #ifdef, never from a
' runtime test -- pnut-ts silently ignores an unknown -D, so a mistyped flag must still land
' on the honest #else token rather than a confident lie.

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-BANNER")
    lineField(@"src_rev", SRC_REV)
    lineField(@"fmt", FMT_VERSION)
#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    lineTextField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgBench)
#else
    lineTextField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgUser)
#endif
#ifdef BENCH_NO_PANEL
    lineTextField(@"panel", @sPanelNo)
#else
    lineTextField(@"panel", @sPanelYes)
#endif
    lineField(@"dwell_floor_s", DWELL_FLOOR_SECS)
    lineField(@"steady_tol_pct", STEADY_TOL_PCT)
    lineField(@"steady_timeout_ms", STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
    lineField(@"pack_nominal_mV", PACK_NOMINAL_MV)
    lineField(@"hold_last", HOLD_LAST)
    lineField(@"clkfreq", CLKFREQ)
    ' The pin bases, voltage and detect mode are compile-time constants in this file rather
    ' than reads of user.*, so that it compiles under every config block (the same rationale
    ' test_bench_t0.spin2 documents). That makes cfg_id alone unable to say WHICH boards were
    ' measured, so the banner states the hardware identity outright: a log is attributable to
    ' hardware on its own evidence, never by inference from which -D was believed to be set.
    lineField(@"left_base", LEFT_TEST_BASE)
    lineField(@"right_base", RIGHT_TEST_BASE)
    lineField(@"voltage_enum", TEST_VOLTAGE)
    lineField(@"det_mode", TEST_DET_MODE)
    lineField(@"panel_w", PANEL_W)
    lineField(@"panel_h", PANEL_H)
    lineField(@"qtr_incre", QTR_SPEED_INCRE)
    lineField(@"half_incre", HALF_SPEED_INCRE)
    lineEmit()

    debug("* PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4)")

PRI preflightWheels() : bOk | side, before, after, moved
' Prove each declared wheel can actually turn before committing the session to nine holds.
'
' WHY THIS IS NOT A getBoardType() CHECK: detection is the thing this sprint is investigating,
' so validating the configuration with it would be circular. Motion is independent -- command
' the wheel briefly and see whether its hall ticks move. On 2026-09-11 the bench config named a
' pin group with no board on it, and nine holds ran against it before anyone noticed.
'
' @returns bOk - TRUE when both declared wheels moved
'
' @local side - SIDE_LEFT then SIDE_RIGHT
' @local before - hall ticks before the nudge
' @local after - hall ticks after the nudge
' @local moved - signed tick delta across the nudge

    bOk := TRUE
    repeat side from SIDE_LEFT to SIDE_RIGHT
        ensureSide(side)
        before := activeHallTicks(side)
        commandMotor(side, PREFLIGHT_INCRE)
        waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS)
        after := activeHallTicks(side)
        commandMotor(side, 0)
        waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS)
        moved := after - before
        debug("BC-PREFLIGHT,side,", udec_(side), ",base,", udec_((side == SIDE_LEFT) ? LEFT_TEST_BASE : RIGHT_TEST_BASE), ",ticks,", sdec_(moved), ",ok,", udec_(moved <> 0))
        if moved == 0
            bOk := FALSE
            debug("!  wheel on that pin group did NOT turn -- wrong pin group, or wiring, or a dead board")

PRI runAllHolds() | holdIdx
' Run every configured hold in sequence, quiescent zero through HOLD_LAST.
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold currently running

    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_ZERO to HOLD_LAST
        runOneHold(holdIdx)

PRI runOneHold(holdIdx) | side, sign, speedIncre, pCaption, pMotorTok, pDirTok, pRungTok, ...
    motorIncre, steadySrcTok, tSteadyMs, tickRate, dwellSecs, pAdvancedByTok, earlyPresses, ...
    pHoldOutcomeTok, iMinMv, iMaxMv, iAvgMv, sampleCount, lastDuty, lastErr, lastDrvState
' Run one hold end to end: announce it, command the motor, wait for steady state, run the
' interactive dwell loop, then log the sense summary and the advance record.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold to run
'
' @local side - SIDE_* the hold drives, or SIDE_NONE for the quiescent-zero hold
' @local sign - +1 forward, -1 reverse, 0 for the quiescent-zero hold
' @local speedIncre - unsigned motor-increment magnitude for this hold's rung
' @local pCaption - pointer to this hold's on-screen/log caption
' @local pMotorTok - pointer to this hold's motor token (NONE/LEFT/RIGHT)
' @local pDirTok - pointer to this hold's direction token (ZERO/FWD/REV)
' @local pRungTok - pointer to this hold's speed-rung token (ZERO/QTR/HALF)
' @local motorIncre - signed motor increment actually commanded (sign * speedIncre)
' @local steadySrcTok - pointer to the steady-state source token (RAMPED/TIMEOUT/ZEROCMD)
' @local tSteadyMs - milliseconds from command issue to steady-state declaration
' @local tickRate - hall-tick rate observed at steady-state declaration
' @local dwellSecs - actual seconds from steady state to acknowledgement
' @local pAdvancedByTok - pointer to the advance-source token (MOUSE/KEY/KEYNP)
' @local earlyPresses - ignored-click count for this hold
' @local pHoldOutcomeTok - pointer to the hold outcome token (OK/FAULT)
' @local iMinMv - smallest sense_i_mV sample seen during the dwell
' @local iMaxMv - largest sense_i_mV sample seen during the dwell
' @local iAvgMv - mean sense_i_mV sample over the dwell
' @local sampleCount - number of sense samples averaged into iAvgMv
' @local lastDuty - most recent duty value at dwell exit
' @local lastErr - most recent position-error value at dwell exit
' @local lastDrvState - most recent DCS_* driver state at dwell exit

    side, sign, speedIncre, pCaption, pMotorTok, pDirTok, pRungTok := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    emitSheet(holdIdx, pCaption)

    ensureSide(side)
    motorIncre := sign * speedIncre
    commandMotor(side, motorIncre)
    emitHoldEntry(holdIdx, pCaption, pMotorTok, pDirTok, pRungTok, motorIncre)

    steadySrcTok, tSteadyMs, tickRate := waitForSteady(side, motorIncre)
    emitSteady(holdIdx, steadySrcTok, tSteadyMs, tickRate)

    dwellSecs, pAdvancedByTok, earlyPresses, pHoldOutcomeTok, iMinMv, iMaxMv, iAvgMv, ...
        sampleCount, lastDuty, lastErr, lastDrvState := runDwellLoop(holdIdx, side, pCaption)

    emitSense(holdIdx, iMinMv, iMaxMv, iAvgMv, sampleCount, lastDuty, lastErr, lastDrvState)
    emitAdvance(holdIdx, dwellSecs, DWELL_FLOOR_SECS, tSteadyMs / MS_PER_SEC, pAdvancedByTok, ...
        earlyPresses, pHoldOutcomeTok)

    if pHoldOutcomeTok == @sResultFault
        emitFault(holdIdx, dwellSecs, lastDrvState, iMaxMv)
        clearActiveFault(side)
        commandMotor(side, 0)

PRI holdInfo(holdIdx) : side, sign, speedIncre, pCaption, pMotorTok, pDirTok, pRungTok
' Return the fixed description of one hold. This is the single source of truth for the hold
' sequence's per-hold shape -- side, direction, speed rung, and every token used in its log
' records.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier to describe
' @returns side - SIDE_* the hold drives
' @returns sign - +1 forward, -1 reverse, 0 for the quiescent-zero hold
' @returns speedIncre - unsigned motor-increment magnitude for this hold's rung
' @returns pCaption - pointer to this hold's caption text
' @returns pMotorTok - pointer to this hold's motor token
' @returns pDirTok - pointer to this hold's direction token
' @returns pRungTok - pointer to this hold's speed-rung token

    case holdIdx
        HOLD_ZERO:
            side := SIDE_NONE
            sign := 0
            speedIncre := 0
            pCaption := @sHold0Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotNone
            pDirTok := @sDirZero
            pRungTok := @sRungZero
        HOLD_L_FWD_QTR:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold1Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotLeft
            pDirTok := @sDirFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_L_REV_QTR:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold2Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotLeft
            pDirTok := @sDirRev
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_R_FWD_QTR:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold3Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotRight
            pDirTok := @sDirFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_R_REV_QTR:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold4Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotRight
            pDirTok := @sDirRev
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_L_FWD_HALF:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold5Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotLeft
            pDirTok := @sDirFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        HOLD_L_REV_HALF:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold6Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotLeft
            pDirTok := @sDirRev
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        HOLD_R_FWD_HALF:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold7Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotRight
            pDirTok := @sDirFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        other:                                               ' HOLD_R_REV_HALF
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold8Caption
            pMotorTok := @sMotRight
            pDirTok := @sDirRev
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf

PRI ensureSide(side)
' Bring exactly the requested wheel's driver cog up, and make certain the other wheel has no
' driver cog at all -- the idle wheel floats by construction, never by being started and told
' to hold. stop() on the outgoing side releases its pin claim and pinclears its driven half,
' which is what makes the outgoing wheel's bridges float during the incoming wheel's holds.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* the caller is about to drive

    if side <> currentSide
        if currentSide == SIDE_LEFT
            wheelL.stop()
        elseif currentSide == SIDE_RIGHT
            wheelR.stop()
        currentSide := side
        if side == SIDE_LEFT
            wheelL.start(LEFT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
            waitUntilReady(side)
        elseif side == SIDE_RIGHT
            wheelR.start(RIGHT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
            waitUntilReady(side)

PRI waitUntilReady(side) | waitedMs
' Wait for the just-started driver cog to report ready, the same pattern
' util_char_motor.spin2:432-444 (waitUntilMotorReady) uses, bounded here rather than looped
' forever so a cog that never comes up cannot hang the whole bench run.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT, the wheel just started
'
' @local waitedMs - milliseconds waited so far

    waitedMs := 0
    repeat until isSideReady(side) or (waitedMs >= STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
        waitms(2)
        waitedMs += 2

PRI isSideReady(side) : bReady
' Report whether the named wheel's driver cog is ready.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bReady - TRUE when that wheel's isReady() is TRUE

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        bReady := wheelR.isReady()
    else
        bReady := wheelL.isReady()

PRI commandMotor(side, motorIncre)
' Command a signed motor increment directly -- the TESTING USE raw-increment path, never
' driveAtPower()'s [-100..100] mapping, and never followed by stopAfterTime(): the motor
' holds at this increment until explicitly recommanded.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* to command; SIDE_NONE commands nothing (both wheels stay unstarted)
' @param motorIncre - signed motor increment to drive at

    if side == SIDE_LEFT
        wheelL.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(motorIncre)
    elseif side == SIDE_RIGHT
        wheelR.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(motorIncre)

PRI activeHallTicks(side) : nPos
' Read raw hall ticks from the wheel currently under test. SIDE_NONE and SIDE_LEFT both read
' wheelL, which for SIDE_NONE (never started) legitimately returns 0.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @returns nPos - raw hall-tick position from getRawHallTicks()

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nPos := wheelR.getRawHallTicks()
    else
        nPos := wheelL.getRawHallTicks()

PRI activeTelemetry(side) : nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault
' Snapshot the wheel currently under test's per-cycle driver status.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @returns nDuty - latest duty value
' @returns nErr - latest position-error value
' @returns nSenseI - latest current-sense reading, in mV, raw and unconverted
' @returns eDrvrState - DCS_* driver state
' @returns bDidFault - TRUE when the driver has faulted

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelR.testGetTelemetry()
    else
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelL.testGetTelemetry()

PRI activeIsFaulted(side) : bFaulted
' Report whether the wheel currently under test has signalled a fault.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @returns bFaulted - TRUE when that wheel's isFaultSignal() is TRUE

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        bFaulted := wheelR.isFaultSignal()
    else
        bFaulted := wheelL.isFaultSignal()

PRI clearActiveFault(side)
' Clear a fault on the wheel currently under test, the same pattern
' util_char_motor.spin2:324-336 (clearFault) uses, without the motion-jog recovery step --
' this harness never needs to recover a working offset, it only needs the fault flag cleared
' so the run can move on to the next hold.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        if wheelR.isFaultSignal()
            wheelR.testResetFault()
    else
        if wheelL.isFaultSignal()
            wheelL.testResetFault()

PRI shutdownMotors()
' Bring both wheels to a safe floating stop at the end of the run.

    if currentSide == SIDE_LEFT
        wheelL.stop()
    elseif currentSide == SIDE_RIGHT
        wheelR.stop()
    currentSide := SIDE_NONE

PRI waitForSteady(side, cmdIncre) : steadySrcTok, elapsedMs, tickRate | prevPos, curPos, ...
    prevRate, curRate, consecCount, bTimedOut, diffPct
' Declare steady state either instantly (the quiescent-zero hold, ZEROCMD) or once
' STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES consecutive hall-tick-rate samples agree within STEADY_TOL_PCT, or
' at STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS regardless (declare steady anyway, source TIMEOUT).
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @param cmdIncre - signed motor increment just commanded; 0 selects the ZEROCMD path
' @returns steadySrcTok - pointer to RAMPED / TIMEOUT / ZEROCMD
' @returns elapsedMs - milliseconds from command issue to this steady-state declaration
' @returns tickRate - hall-tick rate observed at the declaration (0 for ZEROCMD)
'
' @local prevPos - hall-tick position at the previous sample
' @local curPos - hall-tick position at the current sample
' @local prevRate - hall-tick rate at the previous sample, -1 before the first sample
' @local curRate - hall-tick rate at the current sample
' @local consecCount - consecutive samples agreeing within STEADY_TOL_PCT
' @local bTimedOut - TRUE once STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS has elapsed without confirmation
' @local diffPct - percent difference between curRate and prevRate

    if cmdIncre == 0
        steadySrcTok := @sSteadyZerocmd
        elapsedMs := 0
        tickRate := 0
    else
        prevPos := activeHallTicks(side)
        prevRate := -1
        consecCount := 0
        elapsedMs := 0
        bTimedOut := FALSE
        repeat
            waitms(STEADY_SAMPLE_MS)
            elapsedMs += STEADY_SAMPLE_MS
            curPos := activeHallTicks(side)
            curRate := absValue(curPos - prevPos) * (MS_PER_SEC / STEADY_SAMPLE_MS)
            prevPos := curPos
            if prevRate == -1
                consecCount := 1
            elseif prevRate == 0
                consecCount := (curRate == 0) ? consecCount + 1 : 1
            else
                diffPct := (absValue(curRate - prevRate) * 100) / prevRate
                consecCount := (diffPct <= STEADY_TOL_PCT) ? consecCount + 1 : 1
            prevRate := curRate
            bTimedOut := (elapsedMs >= STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
        until (consecCount >= STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES) or bTimedOut
        tickRate := curRate
        steadySrcTok := bTimedOut ? @sSteadyTimeout : @sSteadyRamped

PRI absValue(signedVal) : magnitude
' Return the absolute value of a signed number.
'
' @param signedVal - value to make non-negative
' @returns magnitude - |signedVal|

    magnitude := (signedVal < 0) ? (0 - signedVal) : signedVal

PRI runDwellLoop(holdIdx, side, pCaption) : dwellSecs, pAdvancedByTok, earlyPresses, ...
    pHoldOutcomeTok, iMinMv, iMaxMv, iAvgMv, sampleCount, lastDuty, lastErr, lastDrvState | ...
    elapsedDwellMs, bGateOpen, bAdvanceRequested, btnState, ackUntilMs, flashUntilMs, ...
    nextPanelMs, nextSenseMs, senseSumMv, senseDisplayMv, remainMs, counterVal, ...
    bCounterFlash, barPct, curSenseMv, curDuty, curErr, curDrvState, bFaulted, keyEvent, ...
    mouseClickNow

' Poll mouse, keyboard, sense telemetry and the fault flag every DWELL_POLL_MS until the
' operator's acknowledgement is both requested and permitted, or the driver faults. The dwell
' clock (elapsedDwellMs) starts at 0 here -- at steady state, not at the prompt (BC-HOLD was
' already emitted by the caller before waitForSteady() ran).
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold in progress
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @param pCaption - pointer to this hold's caption text
' @returns dwellSecs - actual seconds from steady state to acknowledgement (or to fault)
' @returns pAdvancedByTok - pointer to MOUSE / KEY / KEYNP, meaningless when pHoldOutcomeTok
'                            is FAULT
' @returns earlyPresses - ignored-click/keypress count during this hold's inert period
' @returns pHoldOutcomeTok - pointer to OK or FAULT
' @returns iMinMv - smallest sense_i_mV sample seen
' @returns iMaxMv - largest sense_i_mV sample seen
' @returns iAvgMv - mean sense_i_mV sample over the dwell
' @returns sampleCount - number of sense samples averaged into iAvgMv
' @returns lastDuty - most recent duty value at exit
' @returns lastErr - most recent position-error value at exit
' @returns lastDrvState - most recent DCS_* driver state at exit
'
' @local elapsedDwellMs - software-accumulated milliseconds since steady state (never a raw
'                          CNT delta -- a 25+ second interval exceeds the signed-CNT-delta
'                          safe window at 270 MHz)
' @local bGateOpen - the ONE place in this file the dwell floor is computed
' @local bAdvanceRequested - set by the mouse path or the keyboard path, never by the gate
' @local btnState - PNL_BTN_INERT / PNL_BTN_LIVE / PNL_BTN_ACK for this frame
' @local ackUntilMs - elapsedDwellMs value at which the ACK visual feedback ends
' @local flashUntilMs - elapsedDwellMs value at which an early-press counter flash ends
' @local nextPanelMs - elapsedDwellMs value at which the panel is next redrawn
' @local nextSenseMs - elapsedDwellMs value at which the on-screen sense mean next updates
' @local senseSumMv - running sum of sense_i_mV samples this hold
' @local senseDisplayMv - the on-screen sense mV value, updated at SENSE_MEAN_UPDATE_MS
' @local remainMs - milliseconds remaining to the dwell floor, for the countdown display
' @local counterVal - the large on-screen digits: seconds remaining or seconds held
' @local bCounterFlash - TRUE while an early-press flash is active
' @local barPct - dwell-bar fill percentage, 0..100
' @local curSenseMv - this poll's raw sense_i_mV sample
' @local curDuty - this poll's duty sample
' @local curErr - this poll's position-error sample
' @local curDrvState - this poll's DCS_* driver state sample
' @local bFaulted - this poll's fault-signal sample
' @local keyEvent - TRUE when this poll saw a new, armed G/g keypress
' @local mouseClickNow - TRUE when this poll saw a new left-button press edge

    elapsedDwellMs := 0
    bAdvanceRequested := FALSE
    pAdvancedByTok := @sAdvKeynp
    earlyPresses := 0
    ackUntilMs := 0
    flashUntilMs := 0
    nextPanelMs := 0
    nextSenseMs := 0
    senseSumMv := 0
    senseDisplayMv := 0
    sampleCount := 0
    iMinMv := POSX
    iMaxMv := NEGX
    lastDuty := 0
    lastErr := 0
    lastDrvState := 0
    pHoldOutcomeTok := @sResultOk

    repeat
        waitms(DWELL_POLL_MS)
        elapsedDwellMs += DWELL_POLL_MS

        curDuty, curErr, curSenseMv, curDrvState, bFaulted := activeTelemetry(side)
        lastDuty := curDuty
        lastErr := curErr
        lastDrvState := curDrvState
        sampleCount += 1
        senseSumMv += curSenseMv
        iMinMv := iMinMv <# curSenseMv
        iMaxMv := iMaxMv #> curSenseMv

        ' -- THE ONE PLACE THE DWELL FLOOR IS COMPUTED --
        bGateOpen := (elapsedDwellMs >= (DWELL_FLOOR_SECS * MS_PER_SEC)) ? TRUE : FALSE

        keyEvent := pollKeyEdge()
        mouseClickNow := FALSE
#ifndef BENCH_NO_PANEL
        mouseClickNow := pollMouseEdge(holdIdx)
#endif

        if bFaulted
            pHoldOutcomeTok := @sResultFault
        elseif mouseClickNow and buttonHit(mouseXpos, mouseYpos)
            if bGateOpen and (bAdvanceRequested == FALSE)
                bAdvanceRequested := TRUE
                pAdvancedByTok := @sAdvMouse
                ackUntilMs := elapsedDwellMs + BTN_ACK_HOLD_MS
            elseif bGateOpen == FALSE
                earlyPresses += 1
                flashUntilMs := elapsedDwellMs + EARLY_FLASH_MS
                emitEarly(holdIdx, (DWELL_FLOOR_SECS * MS_PER_SEC - elapsedDwellMs) / MS_PER_SEC, @sAdvMouse)
        elseif keyEvent
            if bGateOpen and (bAdvanceRequested == FALSE)
                bAdvanceRequested := TRUE
#ifdef BENCH_NO_PANEL
                pAdvancedByTok := @sAdvKeynp
#else
                pAdvancedByTok := @sAdvKey
#endif
                ackUntilMs := elapsedDwellMs + BTN_ACK_HOLD_MS
            elseif bGateOpen == FALSE
                earlyPresses += 1
                flashUntilMs := elapsedDwellMs + EARLY_FLASH_MS
                emitEarly(holdIdx, (DWELL_FLOOR_SECS * MS_PER_SEC - elapsedDwellMs) / MS_PER_SEC, @sAdvKey)

        if elapsedDwellMs >= nextSenseMs
            senseDisplayMv := (sampleCount > 0) ? (senseSumMv / sampleCount) : 0
            nextSenseMs += SENSE_MEAN_UPDATE_MS

        if elapsedDwellMs >= nextPanelMs
            bCounterFlash := (elapsedDwellMs <= flashUntilMs)
            if bGateOpen == FALSE
                remainMs := (DWELL_FLOOR_SECS * MS_PER_SEC) - elapsedDwellMs
                counterVal := (remainMs + MS_PER_SEC - 1) / MS_PER_SEC
                barPct := (elapsedDwellMs * 100) / (DWELL_FLOOR_SECS * MS_PER_SEC)
                btnState := PNL_BTN_INERT
            else
                counterVal := elapsedDwellMs / MS_PER_SEC
                barPct := 100
                btnState := (elapsedDwellMs <= ackUntilMs) ? PNL_BTN_ACK : PNL_BTN_LIVE
            drawPanel(holdIdx, pCaption, counterVal, bCounterFlash, barPct, btnState, ...
                statusToken(side, bFaulted), senseDisplayMv)
            nextPanelMs += PANEL_REDRAW_MS

    until (pHoldOutcomeTok == @sResultFault) or (bGateOpen and bAdvanceRequested)

    if pHoldOutcomeTok == @sResultOk
        waitms(BTN_ACK_HOLD_MS)

    dwellSecs := elapsedDwellMs / MS_PER_SEC
    iAvgMv := (sampleCount > 0) ? (senseSumMv / sampleCount) : 0

PRI statusToken(side, bFaulted) : pStatusTok
' Choose the status-chip token for the current frame.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @param bFaulted - this frame's fault-signal sample
' @returns pStatusTok - pointer to ZERO COMMAND / MOTOR RUNNING / DRIVER FAULT

    if bFaulted
        pStatusTok := @sStatFault
    elseif side == SIDE_NONE
        pStatusTok := @sStatZero
    else
        pStatusTok := @sStatRunning

PRI pollKeyEdge() : bPressed
' Read pc_key and edge-detect a G/g press. pc_key(@keyCode) is always the LAST command in its
' own debug() call, per the panel's input-reading rule. The latch auto-clears after about
' 100 ms; bKeyArmed requires a 0 reading before the next press can register, so a single
' physical keydown cannot be read as two presses while its latch is still set.
'
' @returns bPressed - TRUE on a newly-armed G/g press this poll

    debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))                        ' own backtick -- see test_dog_panel.spin2:204
    bPressed := FALSE
    if keyCode == 0
        bKeyArmed := TRUE
    elseif ((keyCode == "G") or (keyCode == "g")) and bKeyArmed
        bPressed := TRUE
        bKeyArmed := FALSE

#ifndef BENCH_NO_PANEL
PRI pollMouseEdge(holdIdx) : bClicked | rawX, rawY, pInZoneTok
' Read pc_mouse and edge-detect a left-button press. pc_mouse(@mouseXpos) is always the LAST
' command in its own debug() call. Buttons read -1 when pressed; mid/right are read and
' discarded so a stray right-click can never advance a hold. The first MAX_CLICK_LOG clicks
' of the whole run are logged raw, proving the CARTESIAN 1 coordinate basis empirically
' rather than merely asserting it.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold in progress
' @returns bClicked - TRUE on a newly-pressed left button this poll
'
' @local rawX - this poll's raw mouseXpos, captured before any other read can change it
' @local rawY - this poll's raw mouseYpos
' @local pInZoneTok - pointer to "1" or "0", whether the click landed in the button zone

    debug(`bench `pc_mouse(@mouseXpos))                     ' own backtick -- see test_dog_panel.spin2:215
    bClicked := (mouseLtButton == -1) and (prevMouseLt <> -1)
    prevMouseLt := mouseLtButton

    if bClicked and (clickLogCount < MAX_CLICK_LOG)
        rawX := mouseXpos
        rawY := mouseYpos
        pInZoneTok := buttonHit(rawX, rawY) ? @sInZoneYes : @sInZoneNo
        emitClick(holdIdx, rawX, rawY, pInZoneTok)
        clickLogCount += 1
#endif

PRI buttonHit(px, py) : bInside
' Hit-test a point against the button zone, in the same CARTESIAN 1 screen-native basis this
' file draws in -- no inversion needed, per ruling R2.
'
' @param px - x coordinate to test
' @param py - y coordinate to test
' @returns bInside - TRUE when (px, py) falls inside the button rectangle

    bInside := (px >= BTN_X) and (px <= (BTN_X + BTN_W)) and (py >= BTN_Y) and (py <= (BTN_Y + BTN_H))

PRI drawPanel(holdIdx, pCaption, counterVal, bCounterFlash, barPct, btnState, pStatusTok, senseMv) | modeCell, statCell, dgtRow, digits, idx, cell, bLeading
' Compose one frame by blitting opaque cells over the background, then one UPDATE.
'
' Every cell exactly covers its well in bc_bg.bmp, so no erase step is needed -- the new cell
' overwrites the old one. That is the whole economy of the crop-and-overlay technique
' (test_dog_panel.spin2:422-426 is the same shape).
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier, selects the caption cell
' @param pCaption - caption text, used only by the NO_PANEL build
' @param counterVal - seconds remaining (dwell) or seconds held (post-floor)
' @param bCounterFlash - TRUE while an ignored-click flash is active
' @param barPct - retained for the NO_PANEL record; no bar is drawn
' @param btnState - PNL_BTN_INERT / PNL_BTN_LIVE / PNL_BTN_ACK
' @param pStatusTok - pointer to the status-chip token, mapped to a cell below
' @param senseMv - running mean sense mV; logged, not displayed
'
' @local modeCell - LBL_MODE_* cell index for the mode label
' @local statCell - LBL_STAT_* cell index for the status chip
' @local dgtRow - digit sheet row: normal amber, or white while flashing
' @local digits - counterVal clamped to the three digit positions
' @local idx - digit position, 0 is the hundreds column
' @local cell - digit glyph index, or DGT_BLANK for a suppressed leading zero
' @local bLeading - TRUE while still in the leading-zero run

#ifdef BENCH_NO_PANEL
    debug("BC-UI,hold,", udec_(holdIdx), ",caption,", zstr_(pCaption), ",counter,", udec_(counterVal), ",btn,", udec_(btnState))
#else
    modeCell := (btnState == PNL_BTN_INERT) ? LBL_MODE_DWELL : LBL_MODE_HELD

    statCell := LBL_STAT_ZERO
    if pStatusTok == @sStatFault
        statCell := LBL_STAT_FAULT
    elseif pStatusTok == @sStatRunning
        statCell := LBL_STAT_RUN

    dgtRow := bCounterFlash ? DGT_ROW_FLASH : DGT_ROW_NORM

    debug(`bench CROP `(LYR_CAP, 0, holdIdx * CAP_H, CAP_W, CAP_H, CAP_X, CAP_Y))
    debug(`bench CROP `(LYR_LBL, 0, modeCell * LBL_H, LBL_W, LBL_H, MODE_X, MODE_Y))
    debug(`bench CROP `(LYR_LBL, 0, statCell * LBL_H, LBL_W, LBL_H, CHIP_X, CHIP_Y))

    digits := counterVal <# 999
    bLeading := TRUE
    repeat idx from 0 to DGT_COUNT - 1
        cell := digits / decPlaceValue(DGT_COUNT - 1 - idx) // 10
        if (cell <> 0) or (idx == DGT_COUNT - 1)
            bLeading := FALSE
        debug(`bench CROP `(LYR_DGT, (bLeading ? DGT_BLANK : cell) * DGT_W, dgtRow, DGT_W, DGT_H, DGT_X + idx * DGT_PITCH, DGT_Y))

    drawButton(btnState)
    debug(`bench UPDATE)
#endif

PRI decPlaceValue(power) : placeValue
' Return 10 raised to `power`, for splitting the counter into digit columns without a
' floating-point or lookup dependency.
'
' @param power - 0, 1 or 2
' @returns placeValue - 1, 10 or 100

    placeValue := 1
    repeat power
        placeValue *= 10

PRI drawButton(btnState)
' Blit the button cell for the given state. No UPDATE here -- drawPanel owns the frame and
' issues the single UPDATE that shows it.
'
' @param btnState - PNL_BTN_INERT / PNL_BTN_LIVE / PNL_BTN_ACK

#ifndef BENCH_NO_PANEL
    debug(`bench CROP `(LYR_BTN, 0, btnState * BTN_H, BTN_W, BTN_H, BTN_X, BTN_Y))
#endif

PRI drawIdlePanel()
' Final screen once the sequence completes. Restores the untouched background, so no stale
' hold caption or live-looking button is left on screen.

    debug("* BENCH CHAR RUN COMPLETE -- safe to disconnect")
#ifndef BENCH_NO_PANEL
    debug(`bench CROP 1)
    debug(`bench UPDATE)
#endif

PRI emitSheet(holdIdx, pCaption)
' Emit BC-SHEET once per hold, up front, so the operator's paper sheet and this log share row
' numbering.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param pCaption - pointer to this hold's caption text

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-SHEET")
    lineField(@"row", holdIdx + 1)
    lineTextField(@"name", pCaption)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitHoldEntry(holdIdx, pCaption, pMotorTok, pDirTok, pRungTok, cmdIncre)
' Emit BC-HOLD -- this is the task body's "print HOLD,<test>,<rung>".
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param pCaption - pointer to this hold's caption text
' @param pMotorTok - pointer to the motor token
' @param pDirTok - pointer to the direction token
' @param pRungTok - pointer to the speed-rung token
' @param cmdIncre - signed motor increment just commanded

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-HOLD")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineTextField(@"name", pCaption)
    lineTextField(@"motor", pMotorTok)
    lineTextField(@"dir", pDirTok)
    lineTextField(@"rung", pRungTok)
    lineField(@"cmd_incre", cmdIncre)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSteady(holdIdx, pSteadySrcTok, tSteadyMs, tickRate)
' Emit BC-STEADY at steady-state declaration.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param pSteadySrcTok - pointer to RAMPED / TIMEOUT / ZEROCMD
' @param tSteadyMs - milliseconds from command issue to this declaration
' @param tickRate - hall-tick rate observed at the declaration

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-STEADY")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineTextField(@"steady_src", pSteadySrcTok)
    lineField(@"t_steady_ms", tSteadyMs)
    lineField(@"tick_rate", tickRate)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitClick(holdIdx, rawX, rawY, pInZoneTok)
' Emit BC-CLICK for one of the first MAX_CLICK_LOG clicks of the run, proving the coordinate
' basis empirically.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold in progress
' @param rawX - raw mouseXpos at the click
' @param rawY - raw mouseYpos at the click
' @param pInZoneTok - pointer to "1" or "0"

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-CLICK")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineField(@"raw_x", rawX)
    lineField(@"raw_y", rawY)
    lineTextField(@"in_zone", pInZoneTok)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitEarly(holdIdx, remainSecs, pSrcTok)
' Emit BC-EARLY for one ignored press during the inert period.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param remainSecs - seconds remaining to the dwell floor at the moment of the press
' @param pSrcTok - pointer to MOUSE or KEY

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-EARLY")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineField(@"remain_s", remainSecs)
    lineTextField(@"src", pSrcTok)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSense(holdIdx, iMinMv, iMaxMv, iAvgMv, sampleCount, duty, err, drvState)
' Emit BC-SENSE at hold exit.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param iMinMv - smallest sense_i_mV sample seen
' @param iMaxMv - largest sense_i_mV sample seen
' @param iAvgMv - mean sense_i_mV sample over the dwell
' @param sampleCount - number of sense samples averaged
' @param duty - most recent duty value at exit
' @param err - most recent position-error value at exit
' @param drvState - most recent DCS_* driver state at exit

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-SENSE")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineField(@"i_mV_min", iMinMv)
    lineField(@"i_mV_max", iMaxMv)
    lineField(@"i_mV_avg", iAvgMv)
    lineField(@"samples", sampleCount)
    lineField(@"duty", duty)
    lineField(@"err", err)
    lineField(@"drv_state", drvState)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitAdvance(holdIdx, dwellSecs, floorSecs, promptToSteadySecs, pAdvancedByTok, earlyPresses, pHoldOutcomeTok)
' Emit BC-ADV at hold exit. dwellSecs is the actual seconds from steady state to
' acknowledgement, which is what makes the floor auditable after the run rather than merely
' enforced during it -- a dwellSecs below floorSecs is a finding about the instrument.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param dwellSecs - actual seconds from steady state to acknowledgement
' @param floorSecs - DWELL_FLOOR_SECS, so every record states the floor it ran under
' @param promptToSteadySecs - seconds from command issue to steady-state declaration
' @param pAdvancedByTok - pointer to MOUSE / KEY / KEYNP
' @param earlyPresses - ignored-press tally for this hold
' @param pHoldOutcomeTok - pointer to OK or FAULT

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-ADV")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineField(@"dwell_s", dwellSecs)
    lineField(@"floor_s", floorSecs)
    lineField(@"prompt_to_steady_s", promptToSteadySecs)
    lineTextField(@"advanced_by", pAdvancedByTok)
    lineField(@"early_presses", earlyPresses)
    lineTextField(@"result", pHoldOutcomeTok)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitFault(holdIdx, dwellSecs, drvState, iMvAtFault)
' Emit BC-FAULT when a hold ends in a driver fault.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier
' @param dwellSecs - actual seconds from steady state to the fault
' @param drvState - DCS_* driver state at the fault
' @param iMvAtFault - sense_i_mV sample at the fault (the running max, as a proxy)

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-FAULT")
    lineField(@"hold", holdIdx)
    lineField(@"dwell_s", dwellSecs)
    lineField(@"drv_state", drvState)
    lineField(@"i_mV_at_fault", iMvAtFault)
    lineEmit()

PRI lineReset()
' Begin a new record.

    lineLen := 0
    BYTE[@lineBuf][0] := 0

PRI lineAddChar(charByte)
' Append one character to the record under assembly, silently dropping anything past the
' buffer. Every record in this file is well under LINE_BUF_SIZE; truncation would show as a
' short line in the log rather than as memory corruption.
'
' @param charByte - the character to append

    if lineLen < LINE_BUF_SIZE - 1
        BYTE[@lineBuf][lineLen] := charByte
        lineLen += 1
        BYTE[@lineBuf][lineLen] := 0

PRI lineAddText(pText) | srcIdx
' Append a zero-terminated string to the record under assembly. The loop is bounded as well
' as terminated, so an unterminated source string cannot hang the run.
'
' @param pText - pointer to the text to append
'
' @local srcIdx - index into the source text

    repeat srcIdx from 0 to LINE_BUF_SIZE - 1
        if BYTE[pText][srcIdx] == 0
            quit
        lineAddChar(BYTE[pText][srcIdx])

PRI lineAddNum(numValue) | digitStack[MAX_DEC_DIGITS], digitCount, absMagnitude, digitIdx
' Append a signed decimal number with an underscore every three digits, matching udec_() and
' sdec_() elsewhere in this tree's bench logs.
'
' @param numValue - the value to append
'
' @local digitStack - decimal digits of numValue, least significant first
' @local digitCount - how many entries of digitStack are in use
' @local absMagnitude - magnitude of numValue, consumed by the extraction loop
' @local digitIdx - index into digitStack while emitting

    absMagnitude := numValue
    if numValue < 0
        lineAddChar("-")
        absMagnitude := -numValue

    digitCount := 0
    repeat
        digitStack[digitCount] := absMagnitude // DEC_RADIX
        absMagnitude /= DEC_RADIX
        digitCount += 1
    until (absMagnitude == 0) or (digitCount == MAX_DEC_DIGITS)

    repeat digitIdx from digitCount - 1 to 0
        lineAddChar("0" + digitStack[digitIdx])
        if (digitIdx > 0) and (digitIdx // DIGITS_PER_GROUP == 0)
            lineAddChar("_")

PRI lineField(pFieldName, numValue)
' Append one ",name,<number>" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param numValue - the field's value

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddNum(numValue)

PRI lineTextField(pFieldName, pFieldValue)
' Append one ",name,<token>" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param pFieldValue - pointer to the field's token text

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldValue)

PRI lineEmit()
' Emit the assembled record as exactly one debug line. One debug() statement carries at most
' 255 bytes of debug data; the whole record travels as a single zero-terminated string
' instead so wider records are never silently truncated by that limit.

    debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))

